  "summary": "A small woven bag traditionally used for carrying coca leaves and personal items, featuring distinctive geometric patterns and symbolic designs.",
  "description": "Characterized by small size (typically 15-25 cm) with intricate geometric patterns in contrasting colors, often featuring checkerboard designs and symbolic motifs. These bags are traditionally woven using backstrap looms with techniques that vary by region, serving both practical and ceremonial functions in Andean communities.",
